Today, we met with our client, Liz Miller, to show her our prototype.
It was not quite finished yet since most of us had midterms to focus on.
For my part, I am in charge of the visuals of the prototype.

Just as a quick reminder, Liz wants to showcase the islands’ stories and
connections through an interactive website. 
I came up with the idea of creating an abstract map of the archipelago using
watercolors instead of making accurate maps of each island. 
I drew the islands using watercolor brushes and chose random colors for each one.

When I showed Liz my idea, she suggested that I should have a reason behind each color choice. 
For example, an island might be known for a certain flower, 
so I could use the flower’s color to represent that island. 
I really like this idea because it gives more meaning to the colors and
adds another layer of storytelling to the islands. 
It also makes the visuals more connected to the identity and history of each place.
